sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-bipectinata-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-bipectinata-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-bipectinata-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila bipectinata Turing wavelength at 1.92 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 85.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 closes the four Pass-1 remediations. The seven-point D_u sweep is monotonic (self-test). Equal diffusion with an 0.8% white-noise seed amplifies by 0.0388 while the Turing run amplifies by 89.6. Specimen foreground fraction is 0.3233 at the verifier threshold and differs from the percentile-85 mask. Even-mode Pearson r is 0.99478 against a reference of 1.0; odd-mode RMSE is 0.01287 against 0; KS is 0.125 against 0. The last GIF frame matches the pinned specimen at CV similarity 93.0. Weighted overall is 85.3. Overall 85.3/100 (faithfulness 84.9, reproducibility 86.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scipy 1.18.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_bipectinata_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-bipectinata-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/gif, 3266791 B, 640×480 px, 13 frames, artifact_sha256 1c0014b74396d41aea1c5fed8b925dfed4668c3d0198033eb7281e541fec2fdc (sha256 1c0014b74396d41aea1c5fed8b925dfed4668c3d0198033eb7281e541fec2fdc), spec_fingerprint d5f22a094ff81c9bfb8cec455feea78ef577fb724b6dfb1571cde0d7f6d97c6c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: d5f22a094ff81c9bfb8cec455feea78ef577fb724b6dfb1571cde0d7f6d97c6c; artifact_sha256: 1c0014b74396d41aea1c5fed8b925dfed4668c3d0198033eb7281e541fec2fdc. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-bipectinata-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a finite critical wavenumber can be selected by diffusion. | Schnakenberg 1979: kinetics a - u + u^2 v and b - u^2 v. | Kopp & True 2002, Mishra & Singh 2006, and Hurtado-Gonzales et al. 2014 describe D. bipectinata sex combs. None of them states a 1.92 µm wavenumber. | Gompel et al. 2005 is the predecessor citation for D. biarmipes wing pigment.; reconstructed_in_script: Focal linear wavelength 1.92 µm by solving gamma at D_u = 0.0504 µm^2/s and delta = 31.5. | At 0 Ma, D. biarmipes (D_u × 25/16) selects 2.40 µm and D. buzzatii (D_u × 16/25) selects 1.536 µm. | Saturated activator on the 64×64 grid selects 2.56 µm, which is reported rather than forced back to 1.92.; transfer_boundary: Melanin optical density on the gallery JPEG is a visualization of the activator, not a photograph of a 1.92 µm granule field.; does_not_claim: A wet-lab measurement of 1.92 µm in D. bipectinata. | Stratigraphic ancestry among D. biarmipes, D. bipectinata, and D. buzzatii. | That the catalog DOI 10.1111/j.1525-142X.2005.05044.x belongs to this morphology. It is a zebrafish myostatin paper.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.853"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (Cursor cloud agent, loop 3178 pass 2)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
